# One who studies [[paleontology]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1963|author=Claude Lévy-Strauss|title=Structural Anthropology|publisher=Basic Books|location=New York|page=4
|passage=An alternative approach is to break down cultures into ab-<br> stract elements and to establish, between elements of the same<br> type in different cultures, rather than between cultures themselves,<br> the same kind of relationships of historical descent and progressive<br> differentiation which the '''paleontologist''' sees in the evolution of<br> species.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title={{w|The Sixth Extinction: An Unnatural History}}|year=2014|author=w:Elizabeth Kolbert|publisher=Picador|ISBN=9781250062185|passage=In the late nineteenth century, '''paleontologists''' began to catalog the many curious correspondences exhibited by fossils gathered on different continents.|page=197}}

